# FWMIS Development Rules - Cost Optimization

## Model Selection Priority
- **ALWAYS prioritize free-tier models** to minimize costs
- **Free-tier models**: deepseek-r1-0528, deepseek-v3.1, grok-code-fast-1, gemini-2.5-pro, gpt-5-high
- **Paid models**: Only use when free models fail to deliver robust fixes
- **Default choice**: Use deepseek-r1-0528 or grok-code-fast-1 for Python development

## Cost-Conscious Workflow
- Start with free models for all tasks
- Break complex tasks into smaller chunks
- Use specific, focused requests
- Only escalate to paid models when hitting specific limitations
- Batch related tasks to minimize API calls

## Task-Specific Guidelines
- **Coding**: Use deepseek-r1-0528 for Python development
- **Debugging**: Use grok-code-fast-1 for debugging
- **Testing**: Use free models for test script creation
- **Documentation**: Use free models for README updates
- **Refactoring**: Use free models unless complex architecture changes needed

## Request Format
- Always specify model preference: "Use deepseek-r1-0528 for this task"
- Be specific about scope to avoid over-engineering
- Focus on incremental improvements rather than complete rewrites

## Budget Management
- Monitor usage dashboard regularly
- Set usage alerts if available
- Track which tasks consume the most quota
- Prefer free models for 90%+ of interactions

## Emergency Escalation
- Only use paid models when:
  - Free models consistently fail to solve the problem
  - Complex architectural decisions are required
  - Critical production issues need immediate resolution
  - User explicitly requests paid model for specific reason

## Project Context
- Working on FWMIS (Fruitless and Wasteful Expenditure Management Information System)
- Python/PyQt5 application with SQLite database
- Performance optimizations already implemented
- Focus on incremental improvements and new features
